# oracle: pair_style lj/long/coul/long long off 2.5 with kspace pppm/disp at accuracy 1e-2 (native grid 9 9 9, G 1.0325243), kspace_modify disp/auto yes, and the automatic dispersion G-ewald and mesh (no gewald/disp, no mesh/disp), NVE 10 steps, 108 displaced fcc atoms, 2 types
# Measured with native LAMMPS (b332f28 binary): the automatic dispersion G-ewald is 1.032524267031546 natively and 1.03252426700518 in the engine (2.6e-11 relative, the Newton end point); the mesh 9 9 9 agrees; evdwl at step 0 differs by 5.6e-11 relative (passes the 1e-8 target, fails 1e-12).
# oracle-inputs: w161pd_fcc.data
# native: /home/roy/.local/bin/lmp (b332f28, KSPACE package with pppm/disp, unmodified)
units           lj
atom_style      charge
read_data       w161pd_fcc.data
pair_style      lj/long/coul/long long off 2.5
pair_modify     table 0 table/disp 0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.5 1.1
kspace_style    pppm/disp 1.0e-2
kspace_modify   disp/auto yes
timestep        0.005
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl elong ecoul press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             10
